  "articleBody": "Removing a bathtub might seem like simple demolition, but unexpected structural complications and hidden plumbing challenges can quickly surface once you cut into the surround.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps:\n- Heavy cast-iron construction: Old cast-iron tubs can weigh hundreds of pounds and cannot be easily lifted or hauled down tight residential hallways without specialized dismantling methods and safety gear.\n- Soft subfloors or hidden water damage: If the floor around the tub apron feels spongy, or if removing tile exposes mold or deteriorated wood studs, framing repairs must happen before installing new finishes.\n- Plumbing relocations: Converting a tub into a walk-in shower or moving supply lines requires adjusting rough-in depths, resizing drains, and pulling mandatory trade permits.\n- Waterproofing transitions: Wet walls require specialized backer boards, continuous waterproofing membranes, and tight tile work to keep interior wall cavities dry over the long haul.\n- Tight-access spaces: Mobile homes or compact bathrooms require precise maneuvering to avoid punching holes through finished drywall or crushing exposed plumbing.\n\nWhen you want clean demolition, honest communication, and expert tile and finish carpentry, hiring an experienced contractor saves time and stress. Contact HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to schedule your bathroom renovation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
